  "which_is_authoritative": "label_gain_EXACT_DCG_MATCH",
  "why": "LightGBM uses label_gain[label] DIRECTLY as the DCG numerator (its default [0,1,3,7,15,...] is 2**i - 1). The repository's scorer, evaluation/metrics.dcg, applies 2**relevance - 1 on top of the fractional relevance. To make LightGBM's internal lambdarank objective numerically IDENTICAL to the reported metric, label_gain must therefore be 2**relevance - 1 = [0.0, 0.006956, 0.071773, 1.0], not the raw relevance [0.0, 0.01, 0.10, 1.0]. The Phase 1 brief specified the raw-relevance form; both are trained and reported, but the exact-match form is authoritative because only it makes the answer to 'training gain == evaluation convention?' an unqualified YES. The difference between the two is the S:E gain ratio: 0.0718 (exact) vs 0.10 (linear) -- against 0.4286 in V1.",
